er is probably gonna suit us  better so let's put them further ahead  and put more resources behind them when  it comes to adding law and context to a  character's Watson's of the instrumental  in the creation of the games equation at  the arena is that you know do you have  story beats and they get then assigned  to a character but but like judging by  when they actually come up through  development or those elements kind of  put into the character from the  beginning it depends  so character is usually born from a  mechanical place of defensive character  and then once the abilities are known  then it goes over to concept art and  they kind of figure out where's this  character going to look at it look like  but that's in concert with animators who  need to figure out how this character  gonna emote as well as the writers are  gonna figure out who is  character where'd they come from why do  they fight in the arena so that's a big  hodgepodge back and forth that's a large  part of why the process takes so long  because we're not just trying to give  gay players gameplay we're trying to  give them like something to attach to  emotionally the fact that we have so  much fan art people cause playing our  characters it really shows to me that we  are doing something good in that arena  and players are attaching these  characters and with Watson specifically  being that she is an engineer and she  has these wire lines it's all  electricity based there's a really cool  connection that we could have there of  writing her as the as the one who kind  of figured out how the ring should work  we have a bunch of other stuff that the  world will probably never see like we  have an internal kind of like universe  guide that so as developers at respawn  are working on a piece of content they  can kind of immerse themselves in why  does this thing exist where did it come  from who made it all these things so  that we try and be as consistent as  possible and really create that universe  for players to attach to it's super  interesting I'm fascinated by the idea  like how has respawns like workflow  changed because of Apex legends or like  to adapt to apex legends right it's not  this traditional release model anymore  it's release a game get feedback right  tweak the things in DB tweak plan the  future of the roadmap what has it been  like transitioning into that  specifically from like a workflow  standpoint four or respawned  well it's actually forced us to put a  magnifying glass to some of our  processes that worked fine again we're  trying to converge on one point two and  a half years down the road where there's  a lot of slop that we could soak up but  when you got to do that all the time we  have to find a lot more efficiencies in  our process it's like I was saying  characters taking us a year and a half  that's not gonna be long-term  sustainable we want to be shipping  characters faster than we currently are  so right now we're in a big big process  right now to figure out how can we do  that without crunching our team without  just throwing extra people at the  problem because for us hiring is also a  really slow and somewhat arduous process  we started the team nine years ago with  30 people and now we're only about 120  and it's taking us that long and we've  been hiring constantly  that process we can't just oh wait  here's five hundred resumes hire those  people put them at desks and so it's  really had a profound impact on our our  development processes pipeline tools all  that kind of stuff I can't possibly let  you leave the stage without asking a  couple of questions but I know you won't  building something the answers to but I  have to say you never know number one is  to deal with that big dragon boy what's  the line I was allowed to say a couple  big things are making their way the  Kings came in but I will say I was  following the reddit thread about the  space cows I just keep your eyes peeled  I'll say over the next few weeks okay  and finally I mean so I think I met you  a few years ago when you still on the  titanfall team and obviously respawn is  now working on Star Wars Jedi fallen  order as well as FX legends is there any  hope for people who still are waiting  for that third titanfall game you know I  mean respawn was born out of titanfall  it has a huge amount of identity for the  studio itself and we all love it very  dearly who knows what that comes to in  the future but we definitely care a lot  about titanfall and what it brings to  the game industry thank you so much for  joining us guys make sure if you're  watching at home that you don't go  anywhere  coming up next we're gonna be speaking  with Todd Howard about the future of  fallout 76  [Music]  you
 

